#
# rc(8) load_rc_config only reads /etc/rc.conf.d/<service-name>, so every
# setting lives in a file named after the rc script that consumes it (the
# old misnamed /etc/rc.conf.d/<distro> fragment was never read).
#
# The placeholder is substituted by build.sh (slug, e.g. examplebsd).
hostname="@SLUG@"
